── detail · install and sign in ──
Each agent is its own program with its own sign-in. radar finds it on your PATH; read its status again.

§ :bot: COPILOT  checking
  $ npm i -g @github/copilot  {copy:install:copilot}
  copy command · $ copilot login  (y)  {copy:login:copilot}
  Needs a Copilot plan on GitHub.
  :link:  open documentation · GitHub: install Copilot CLI  (o)
§ :bot: CODEX  checking
  $ npm i -g @openai/codex  {copy:install:codex}
  $ codex login  {copy:login:codex}
  :link:  Codex: install and sign in
§ :bot: CLAUDE AGENT  checking
  $ npm i -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code  {copy:install:claude}
  $ claude auth login  {copy:login:claude}
  radar runs your own claude and offers no sign-in of its own.
  Anthropic does not allow a claude.ai login in a product: for one it asks for an API key (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY).
  :link:  Claude Code: set up
§ :terminal: ANY OTHER CLI
  add a command takes what you would type in a terminal; radar runs it in a tab of the dock.
§ :warning: NOTHING IS APPROVED FOR YOU
  A request waits in the dock for your answer:
  approve · session · deny · view diff
  alt-a switches the agent new sessions start as.
